  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "The 2026 election for Michigan's 13th Congressional District will determine who represents a safely Democratic seat covering much of Detroit and several Downriver suburbs, including Allen Park, Hamtramck, Romulus, and Wyandotte. Incumbent Democrat Shri Thanedar, first elected in 2022, faces a competitive Democratic primary challenge from state Representative Donavan McKinney, who has drawn support from progressive and labor groups. On the Republican side, T.P. Nykoriak is the sole qualified primary candidate, while independent candidate Maurice Morton has also entered the race. The primary election is scheduled for August 4, 2026, and the general election will be held on November 3, 2026.",
